9. Statistical Falsification Criteria

The framework predicts that:

1. Unsafe attractors are unreachable under the compatible CBF-CLF controller with probability at least 1-\delta.
2. The viability margin remains positive with high probability.
3. Attractor identification converges with polynomial sample complexity under basin coverage.

Statistical Protocol:

· Report 95% confidence intervals for each metric across M\ge 10 random seeds.
· Perform two-sided hypothesis tests against the null hypothesis of no safety benefit.
· Conduct ablations: remove each component (CBF, CLF, compatibility, robust margin) and report the resulting change in each metric.
· Falsification occurs if any of the following hold:
  · The upper confidence bound on reachable unsafe attractors exceeds a pre-registered threshold.
  · The lower confidence bound on viability margin is non-positive.
  · Sample complexity grows faster than polynomial in 1/\delta under basin coverage.

