11.4 Integration: A Unified Computational Architecture

The two extensions—adaptive computation allocation and distributionally robust viability—can be integrated into a unified architecture for tractable runtime safety verification.

Algorithm 11.1 (Adaptive Distributionally Robust Safety Filter).

Input: State x_t, parameter estimate \hat{\theta}_t, ambiguity set \mathcal{P}_t, computational budget C_t.

Output: Safe control u_t.

1. Compute safety margin:
   m_t = \min_{x\in\mathcal{C}}\left(B(F_{\hat{\theta}}(x_t,u_{\text{ref}})) - (1-\alpha)B(x_t) - \rho(t) - \delta_{\mathrm{model}}\right).
2. Compute marginal value:
   \mathcal{M}\text{-Val}(x_t,\hat{\theta}_t) = \frac{\partial}{\partial C}\mathbb{P}\left(\text{safety}\mid C_t\right).
3. Allocate computation: If m_t is small or \mathcal{M}\text{-Val} is large, increase verification horizon N and reduce ambiguity radius \rho (by collecting more samples). Otherwise, use a short horizon and a conservative ambiguity set.
4. Solve the distributionally robust QP:
   \begin{aligned}
   \min_{u\in\mathcal{U}}\quad & \|u-u_{\text{ref}}\|^2\\
   \text{s.t.}\quad
   & V(F_{\hat{\theta}}(x_t,u))-V(x_t)\le-\alpha(V(x_t)),\\
   & B(F_{\hat{\theta}}(x_t,u))\ge(1-\alpha)B(x_t)-\rho(t)-\delta_{\mathrm{model}},\\
   & u\in\mathcal{U}_{\mathrm{adm}}.
   \end{aligned}
5. Apply safety filter if the QP is infeasible: use the backup controller from the robust viability kernel.

Theorem 11.5 (Safety of Algorithm 11.1). Under the assumptions of Theorem 11.3 and Proposition 11.1, if the computational budget C_t is sufficient to solve the QP to feasibility, then Algorithm 11.1 guarantees x_t\in\mathcal{V} for all t\ge 0 with probability at least 1-\delta.

Proof. The distributionally robust barrier condition ensures that the QP is feasible whenever the state is in the distributionally robust viability kernel. The adaptive horizon guarantees that the computational budget is allocated where it is most needed. The robust margin ensures that the safety condition holds for the true system. \square

