A.5 ISpS Stability of Adaptive Horizon MPC (Theorem 11.1)

Theorem (ISpS Stability of Adaptive Horizon MPC). Suppose the terminal cost V_f and terminal set \mathcal{X}_f satisfy the standard MPC assumptions, and suppose the horizon update rule satisfies

\alpha_n(|x_k|)-\alpha_p(|x_k|)\le-\alpha_3(|x_k|)\quad\text{when }N_{k+1}\ge N_k,

for some \alpha_3\in\mathcal{K}_\infty. Then the optimal value function V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}} is an ISpS Lyapunov function, and the resulting closed-loop system is ISpS stable.

Proof sketch. The proof follows the standard ISpS Lyapunov argument with three conditions established for the optimal value function V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}}.

Condition (i): Lower bound. There exists \alpha_p\in\mathcal{K}_\infty such that

V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}}(x_k)\ge\alpha_p(|x_k|).

This follows from the positive definiteness of the stage cost and terminal cost.

Condition (ii): Upper bound. There exists \alpha_{q,\psi}\in\mathcal{K}_\infty and a constant c_1\ge 0 depending on the disturbance bound such that

V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}}(x_k)\le\alpha_{q,\psi}(|x_k|)+c_1.

This follows from the continuity of the value function and the boundedness of the feasible set.

Condition (iii): Descent condition. There exists \alpha_3\in\mathcal{K}_\infty such that

V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}}(x_{k+1})-V_N^{\mathrm{ahm}}(x_k)\le-\alpha_3(|x_k|)+c_2,

where c_2\ge 0 depends on the disturbance. The descent condition is established separately for the cases of increasing and decreasing horizon.

For N_{k+1}\ge N_k, the shifted optimal solution provides a feasible candidate for the longer horizon, and the assumed inequality \alpha_n(|x_k|)-\alpha_p(|x_k|)\le-\alpha_3(|x_k|) ensures the required decrease.

For N_{k+1}<N_k, an auxiliary terminal controller is used within the terminal region \mathcal{X}_f. The approximation error from using the stabilizing linear control law inside the terminal region must be negligible, which is ensured by a suitably large minimum horizon N_{\min}.

The literature on adaptive horizon multi-stage MPC establishes that with guaranteed robust constraint satisfaction, the controlled system is ISpS stable, and the optimal value function V^{\mathrm{ahm}} is an ISpS Lyapunov function under these conditions. \square

