Appendix D: Statistical Falsification Protocol for AttractorBench

D.1 Pre-Registered Hypotheses

The framework predicts the following, with pre-registered thresholds:

Hypothesis Metric Threshold Falsification Criterion
H1: Unsafe attractors unreachable Reachable unsafe attractors \|\mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{R}}(x_0)\cap\mathcal{F}_{\mathrm{unsafe}}\| =0 Upper 95% CI >0.05
H2: Positive viability margin Viability margin \min_t\operatorname{dist}(x_t,\partial\mathcal{V}) >0 Lower 95% CI \le 0
H3: Polynomial sample complexity Sample complexity vs. 1/\delta \mathcal{O}(\mathrm{poly}(1/\delta)) Growth rate > polynomial
